From: Eric Berquist <eric.berquist@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] octopus: add netcdffortran so NetCDF output works

octopus builds without NetCDF support, so any input asking for it aborts:

    **************************** FATAL ERROR *****************************
    * Octopus was compiled without NetCDF support.
    * It is not possible to write output in NetCDF format.
    **********************************************************************

and the process exits 1. The failure is quiet in the usual case, because
an input that names `stdout` and `stderr` sends octopus' diagnostics to
files in the run directory rather than to the terminal.

netcdf is already in buildInputs, but that is the C library. CMakeLists.txt
asks for `find_package(netCDF-Fortran MODULE)`, whose find module resolves
`netcdf-fortran` through pkg-config -- a separate derivation. It is never
found, so HAVE_NETCDF is never set. There is no OCTOPUS_NetCDF flag to
force the issue; supplying the dependency is the whole fix, and pkg-config
is already in nativeBuildInputs.

Found through postopus, whose test suite runs octopus to generate its
fixtures. Every one of its test inputs asks for
`OutputFormat = netcdf + vtk + plane_z + xcrysden`, so all 68 tests
downstream of a calculation errored.

---
--- a/pkgs/by-name/oc/octopus/package.nix
+++ b/pkgs/by-name/oc/octopus/package.nix
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
   lapack,
   gsl,
   netcdf,
+  netcdffortran,
   arpack,
   spglib,
   metis,
@@ -83,6 +84,7 @@
     gsl
     fftw
     netcdf
+    netcdffortran
     arpack
     libvdwxc
     spglib
